SIM SYSTEM AS RELATIONAL OBJECT
========================
S_SIM := < V, E, O, G >

V  = entities
E  = relations (edges)
O  = operators
G  = induced geometry

0. LAYERS
---------
SID = spacetime / structure (static)
PED = process / evolution / dynamics (operators on edges)

SID: form-factor metric, EF containment graph,
     identifier types (ICCID, IMSI, Ki, PIN, PUK)

PED: A3/A8/A5, Milenage, Attach, PIN/PUK gate,
     buck + PI loop

RDG: one relational graph, typed edges, operator-labeled
     dynamics, geometry on both physical nodes and
     abstract state spaces

1. SID — STRUCTURAL / GEOMETRIC LAYER
--------------------------------------
1.1 Form-factor nodes
  v_Full, v_Mini, v_Micro, v_Nano, v_eSIM  in  V_SIM

  phi_geom : V_SIM -> R^3
  phi_geom(v) = (w_v, h_v, t_v)

  Full  : (85.6, 54.0, 0.76) mm
  Mini  : (25.0, 15.0, 0.76) mm
  Micro : (15.0, 12.0, 0.76) mm
  Nano  : (12.3,  8.8, 0.67) mm
  eSIM  : embedded (no removable metric)

  Type: static metric embedding
  Fundamentals: ISO/IEC 7810, ETSI TS 102 221

1.2 File-system nodes
  V_FS = { EF_ADN, EF_SMS, EF_LOCI, ... }

  E_contain  subset  V_SIM x V_FS

  Type: containment relation
  Fundamentals: SIM is container; EFs are embedded sub-objects
                gated by access predicates


2. PED — DYNAMIC / OPERATOR LAYER
---------------------------------
2.1 GSM/UMTS authentication
  e_auth : (Network, SIM) |-> AuthState

  A3 : {0,1}^128 x {0,1}^128 -> {0,1}^32
  A8 : {0,1}^128 x {0,1}^128 -> {0,1}^64

  RAND  <-$ {0,1}^128
  SRES  = A3(Ki, RAND)
  Kc    = A8(Ki, RAND)

  (Unauth, RAND) --A3,A8--> (Auth, Kc, SRES)

  Accept <=> (SRES_SIM = SRES_network)

  Type: challenge-response morphism on auth edge
  Fundamentals: Ki never transmitted; only SRES compared

2.2 EPS-AKA / Milenage
  M : (Ki, RAND, OP_C) |-> (RES, Kc)

  TEMP = E_Ki( RAND XOR OP_C )     // E = AES-128
  RES  = out1(TEMP)
  Kc   = out2(TEMP)

  Accept(M) := [ RES = XRES ]

  Type: refined auth operator (same edge, AES geometry)
  Fundamentals: interface-compatible with A3/A8

2.3 Attach / identity evolution
  Attach : IMSI |-> TMSI  or  GUTI

  Type: label-rewriting operator on network-SIM edge
  Fundamentals: public ID replaced by temporary ID after Accept

2.4 PIN/PUK local gate
  e_local : (User, SIM) |-> AccessState

  Unlock <=> (PUK = PUK*) AND (attempts <= 10)
  PIN attempts <= 3 before lock

  Type: local predicate, orthogonal to network auth
  Fundamentals: user-SIM edge only

2.5 Cipher (post-Accept)
  z = A5(Kc, F)
  C = P XOR z

  Type: stream operator driven by session key
  Fundamentals: frame-synchronized once Kc installed

3. OBJECT
-------------
3.1 Nodes
  V = { User, SIM, Network, Controller,
        EF_ADN, EF_SMS, EF_LOCI, ... }

3.2 Edges
  e_auth    : (Network, SIM)     ops = {A3, A8, A5, M}
  e_attach  : (Network, SIM)     ops = {Attach}
  e_local   : (User, SIM)        ops = {PIN_Gate, PUK_Gate}
  e_fs      : (SIM, EF_x)        ops = {ReadAllowed}
  e_power   : (Controller, Phone)   ops = {PI_Controller}

3.3 Operator bundle
  O = { A3, A8, A5, M, Attach,
        PIN_Gate, PUK_Gate, PI_Controller }

  Each operator acts on one typed edge and one state space.

4. GEOMETRIC EMBEDDINGS G
-------------------------
4.1 Card geometry
  G_form : V_SIM -> R^3

4.2 Auth state space
  Sigma_auth = { Unauth, Auth, Locked }
  transitions labeled by A3/A8/M

4.3 Power-stage state space (separate sub-system)
  X_power = { (i_L, v_o) }

  L * di_L/dt = d * v_in - v_o
  C * dv_o/dt = i_L - v_o / R

  d(k) = d(k-1) + Kp*(e(k)-e(k-1)) + Ki*e(k)
  e(k) = v_ref(k) - v_o(k)

  Type: continuous state + discrete duty-cycle controller
  Fundamentals: shares only the Controller node with the SIM graph;
                not part of authentication geometry

